+"""Inference runtime for a saved PrefixQuant artifact (transformers >= 4.51).
+
+What ``main.save_quant_model`` writes: fake-quantized fp16 weights (already on the W4 grid after
+``block_ap.quant_inplace``) and every quantizer scale (``save_pretrained``), the fp16 prefix
+(K, V) of every layer (``prefixed_key_values.safetensors``) and ``prefixequant_config.json``.
+
+``attach_quantization`` rebuilds on a stock model loaded from that directory exactly what the
+quantization run had at the end of ``block_ap`` (the eval.py recipe, with the residual norms
+selected by name so that Qwen3's q_norm/k_norm stay plain): QuantLinear (an nn.Linear
+subclass) for every decoder projection, the A4 output quantizers of the two residual norms, the
+o_proj/down_proj input quantizers, the v_proj output (V cache) quantizer, the R4 online
+Hadamard on the down_proj input, and the R3 Hadamard + K quantizer in the RoPE wrapper (after
+q_norm/k_norm and RoPE). The quantizer mode comes from ``prefixequant_config.json``:
+static (O2) quantizers load their saved ``scale``; dynamic (O1, per-token activations and
+group-wise KV) quantizers compute the range online and, with ``activation_clipping``, load the
+learned per-layer ``bound_factor`` (``upbound_factor``/``lowbound_factor`` when asymmetric).
+The repo builds the K quantizer without clipping, so a dynamic K quantizer has no saved state.
+Weight quantization is not re-applied per forward (the stored weights are already quantized);
+activation and KV quantizers run online.
+
+``install_prefix`` makes the model behave like the calibrated one: every forward that starts a
+sequence gets a fresh, batch-expanded copy of the fp16 prefix KV, real tokens sit at positions
+>= P and the attention mask covers the P prefix columns. Logits, loss and ``generate`` output
+only cover the caller's tokens.
